   {
    "id": "of-title",
    "type": "heading",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-field"
    ],
    "text": "Everything the author wanted on one page"
   },
   {
    "id": "of-para-1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-field"
    ],
    "text": "The first paragraph describes the site in full. It names the open ground, the pale sky and the distant hills, and it explains why the object was placed where it was. It records who visited, on which day, with which instruments, and it states that every number on this page is synthetic. It then describes the approach path, the light at noon and the light at dusk, and the reason the photographs were taken from the left. None of this text is measured or real."
   },
   {
    "id": "of-para-2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-field"
    ],
    "text": "The second paragraph lists what the team wanted to show: the whole object in context, the seam and the latch up close, the loop that regulates the flow, and the two panels that compare the two settings on one scale. It explains that each of these later received a page of its own, that the sequence runs from context to product to detail to mechanism to evidence, and that the closing page asks for three concrete actions rather than a summary. This whole paragraph is illustrative only, as the page says."
   },
   {
    "id": "of-para-3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-field"
    ],
    "text": "The third paragraph explains the rule this page exists to exercise. A page taller than the frame is never shrunk as a whole. The exporter looks for a line no element crosses and cuts there, repeating the heading on the continuation. The author can also move supporting text behind the disclosure, where it remains on the page, in the notes and in the appendix. Either way the words survive on the page and the text stays readable at the declared minimum size."
   },
   {
    "id": "of-list-1",
    "type": "list",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-product"
    ],
    "items": [
     "Context first",
     "Product second",
     "Detail third",
     "Mechanism fourth",
     "Evidence fifth",
     "Action last",
     "No padding pages",
     "No shrunk pages"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "of-list-2",
    "type": "list",
    "sourceIds": [
     "src-product"
    ],
    "items": [
     "Measure before judging",
     "Cut where nothing crosses",
     "Repeat the heading",
     "Keep the strip on the last band",
     "Report the scale",
     "Report the typography",
     "Open the files",
     "Name the weakest page"
    ]
   },
